															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ashton-hennessy" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6459445); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6459445&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608972724" alt="Ashton Hennessy " style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6459445)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ashton-hennessy" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6459445); return false;" >Ashton Hennessy </a></span> <span class="odate time_1590419074 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">25 May 2020 15:04</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4662823">
									

<p>Haha wow &#8212; it's impressive that you trimmed it down that much whilst still keeping the core ideas intact! I'll keep that advice in mind, and try to use some of the techniques you used in trimming down the phrasing.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I get that this SCP is a bit derivative: it's a keter (but not <em>thaaaaaaaaat</em> keter) Fred who's trapped inside of an SCP article! And who's also sassily narrating the article and 'fighting' the Foundation, which is probably a cliche that has entire subreddits dedicated to mocking!</p>
<p>But I think it has a enough subtle how-it-works differences to these two articles &#8212; and <em>largely different</em>, I'd say, narrative differences &#8212; to stand on its own two feet, although it probably requires a bit more tinkering with.</p>
<p>The core idea, anyway, is the SCP's strange worldview and actions in furthering that worldview, which I think is a fairly unique idea (although I understand that the way I wrote about it in the summary as a 'philosophy that I've just invented wowowow' probably doesn't give many critics faith in my ability to execute it!).</p>
<p>I'll decide whether to scrap the idea or just tinker and repost and try again (after it becomes super inactive for a period of time obviously) based on the 'consensus' of how derivative it is from these two ideas, and scan around the related tags to see if there's any even more egregious ripping-offs that I'm doing (and obviously scrap the idea if there are).</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Thank you for taking the time to write all of this useful feedback! :D</p>

							</div>

								
