														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4662041">
									

<p>This is maybe what my <a href="/scp-2323">first article</a> (currently a respectable +186) would have looked like if we had this system at the time:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Dark Fantasy</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> Conventional SCP</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> Some non-anamolous birds have learned to hunt faeries with cold iron. The Foundation can't contain the faeries so they contain the birds.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Con-procs describe the Foundation maintaining a population of shrikes.
<ul>
<li>Shrikes are under conditions that allow them to teach their young and hunt in an aviary enclosure.</li>
<li>Wild instances of birds with this skill are exterminated.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Birds kill invisible things by impaling them on barbed wire.</li>
<li>Bits of tiny tools and clothing, bones and wings are in the bird's guts.</li>
<li>Ending reveals that the faeries are building shrines and making sacrifices to the birds.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>Non-human memetics</li>
<li>Cold-not-cruel allowing birds to hunt sapients in order to maintain containment.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Real shrikes lack talons and use thorns, barbed wire, ect. to kill prey.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
143 words.
<p>Anyone is free to use this example if they want.</p>

							</div>

								
